{
First, compute the remaining capacity after adding the item to each bin, then prioritize bins where the item fits perfectly (remaining capacity 0) highest, followed by bins with positive remaining capacity (where item fits without overfilling) in ascending order of remaining capacity (to favor tight fits), and assign the lowest priority to bins where the item does not fit (negative remaining capacity) ordered by most negative (least overfill) to most overfill.
}

{
New algorithm: Assign priority as the negative of the absolute difference between the bin capacity and the item size, so that bins with capacity closest to the item size receive the highest priority.
